---
// Ported from the Claude Design canvas artboard Blog.dc.html. Edit the canvas, then re-port.
import BaseV2 from '../../layouts/BaseV2.astro';
---
<BaseV2 title="Blog · Paramore.Design" description="Notes on design, building products, and things I’m learning along the way.">
  <section class="pd-wrap" data-screen-label="Header">
    <div class="pd-topline"><span>Blog</span><span style="color: var(--color-text-faint)">2 posts</span></div>
    <h1 class="pd-title" style="margin-top: 40px">Thoughts &amp; Writing</h1>
    <p class="pd-lede" style="margin-top: 28px">Notes on design, building products, and things I’m learning along the way.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="pd-wrap pd-section pd-section--last" data-screen-label="Posts">
    <div class="pd-head" style="margin-bottom: 0"><span class="pd-kicker pd-kicker--accent">Newest first</span></div>

    <a href="/blog/posts/building-tain" class="pd-card" style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(320px, 100%), 1fr)); gap: 24px 48px; padding: 40px 0; border-bottom: var(--pd-rule)">
      <div class="pd-frame" style="max-width: 420px"><img src="/assets/images/blog/building-tain.jpg" alt="Cover for the article on building Tain" style="aspect-ratio: 4 / 5"></div>
      <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px">
        <div style="display: flex; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap"><span class="pd-kicker pd-kicker--accent">Personal Project // Product Design</span><span class="pd-kicker">Jul 25, 2026</span></div>
        <h2 class="pd-card__title" style="font-size: clamp(28px, 3.4vw, 48px)">I Kept Forgetting the Things I Loved, So I Built an App to Remember Them</h2>
        <p class="pd-lede" style="font-size: 18px">A diary of everything I’ve consumed, ranked by comparison, with notes from me to future me. Meet Tain.</p>
        <p class="pd-card__desc">I’ve been through hundreds of audiobooks and I have real opinions about most of them, but when someone asks what to listen to next, my mind goes blank. So I built an app to hold all of it: nine categories, tier boards, and a name twenty-five years in the making.</p>
        <span class="pd-arrow-link">Read article →</span>
      </div>
    </a>

    <a href="/blog/posts/building-with-fable-5" class="pd-card" style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(320px, 100%), 1fr)); gap: 24px 48px; padding: 40px 0; border-bottom: var(--pd-rule)">
      <div class="pd-frame" style="max-width: 420px"><img src="/assets/images/blog/building-with-fable-5.jpg" alt="Cover for the article on building with Fable 5" style="aspect-ratio: 4 / 5"></div>
      <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px">
        <div style="display: flex; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap"><span class="pd-kicker pd-kicker--accent">AI Tools // Game Dev</span><span class="pd-kicker">Jun 16, 2026</span></div>
        <h2 class="pd-card__title" style="font-size: clamp(28px, 3.4vw, 48px)">It’s Easy to Have AI Build Things That Look Finished</h2>
        <p class="pd-lede" style="font-size: 18px">I gave Fable 5 a game I’d failed to build for years, and learned what AI quietly skips.</p>
        <p class="pd-card__desc">The day Fable came out, I handed it screenshots, flow sketches, and design docs, turned on bypass permissions, and walked away. When I came back, a working prototype was running in my browser, and the real lesson was just getting started.</p>
        <span class="pd-arrow-link">Read article →</span>
      </div>
    </a>
  </section>
</BaseV2>
